{title: 393 - Lord of the Sabbath}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #393 • PARK STREET • 16.17.9}
{lyricist: Anon}
{composer: Frederick M. A. Venua}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 393}
{meta: tune PARK STREET}
{meta: meter 16.17.9}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]Lord [F/C]of the Sabbath [C7/Bb]and [C/G]its [Dm/A]light, [F]I hail Thy hallowed [Gm]day [F]of [C/E]rest;
[C/E]It is my [F]weary [Gm]soul's delight, [Am]The solace [Gm]of [Bb/F]mycareworn [F]breast,
[F/A]The solace [G7]of [C7/Bb]my [F]careworn [C/G]breast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]O [F/A]sacred [C7/Bb]day [Dm/A]of [F]peace and joy,
[Dm/A]Thy [F/A]hours are [C/G]ever [F]dear [Gm]to [F]me;
[C/E]Ne'er [F]may [Gm]a [F]sinful [Gm]thought destroy
[F/A]The holy [G7]calm [F]I [C7/Bb]find [Dm/A]in [C/G]thee,
[F/A]The holy [G7]calm [F]I [C7/Bb]find [Dm/A]in [C/G]thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]How [F/A]sweetly [C/G]now [F]they glide [Gm]along!
[Dm/A]How [F/A]hallowed [C/G]is [F]the calm [Gm]they [F]yield!
[C/E]Transporting [Gm]is [Am]their rapturous [C/E]song,
[F/A]And heavenly [C7/Bb]visions seem [Dm/A]revealed,
[F/A]And heavenly [C7/Bb]visions seem [Dm/A]revealed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm/A]O [F/A]Jesus, [C/G]let [F]me ever hail
[Dm/A]Thy [F/A]presence [C/G]with [F]the day [Gm]of [F]rest;
[C/E]Then [F]will [Gm]Thy [F]servant [Gm]never [C/E]fail
[F/A]To deem Thy [G7]Sabbath [C7/Bb]doubly [C/G]blest,
[F/A]To deem Thy [G7]Sabbath [C7/Bb]doubly [C/G]blest.
{end_of_verse}
